text:
morgan: Quick heads-up — onboarding sampleapp failing for embeddings+rerank parity between Node and Python SDKs. Looks like two separate but compounding issues.

reza: short list?

morgan: 1) Node batching helper sometimes returns a nested vector for single-item batches: [[0.1,...]] while Python returns [0.1,...]. 2) Rerank responses vary field name across model versions (we've seen "score", "ranking_score", and now once "rank_score"). 3) Auth retry can resend request without the client-generated idempotency header causing duplicate side effects.

anya: can you paste a tiny repro and a sample server response?

morgan: minimal repro below (abbreviated):

```js
// Node helper
const batch = makeBatch([{text: 'find me'}])
// batch -> [ [0.12, 0.03, ...] ]  // nested for n=1

// Python helper
b = make_batch(['find me'])
# b -> [0.12, 0.03, ...]  // flat

// Rerank server payloads we've seen:
{ "results": [{ "id": "d1", "score": 0.82 }] }
{ "results": [{ "id": "d1", "ranking_score": 0.82 }] }
{ "results": [{ "id": "d1", "rank_score": 0.82 }] }
```

reza: I can repro the Node nesting locally. The helper always wraps outputs, then downstream code wraps again when it expects list-of-list. Quick guard: if batch.length === 1 and Array.isArray(batch[0]) && typeof batch[0][0] === 'number' then flatten or ensure consistent shape.

anya: For rerank key variance, simplest SDK defense is to accept multiple keys with priority: score > ranking_score > rank_score > confidence. We should also add a small schema validation in CI so future model changes fail fast.

infra-bot: Created ticket DEVEX-2729: "sampleapp: embed batch shape mismatch + rerank key variance + auth retry idempotency". Linked requests: node-batchfix, sdk-rerank-mapping, auth-retry-idempotency.

kevin: On auth retries: Node auth middleware refreshes token then resends request but it doesn't preserve x-rw-idempotency-token. Server processes twice for side-effecting endpoints. Fix options: preserve the header across retries, or only refresh token and retry idempotency-safe endpoints. I'd prefer preserving token by default.

morgan: Short-term workaround I pushed to the sampleapp template: normalize embedding shape and map rerank keys on client before calling retriever. Snippet: 

```js
// normalize embeddings
let vecs = resp.data;
if (!Array.isArray(vecs[0])) vecs = [vecs];

// map rerank score
const mapped = res.results.map(r => ({ id: r.id, score: r.score ?? r.ranking_score ?? r.rank_score ?? r.confidence }));
```

reza: I'll open the node PR to make the helper return a consistent shape for single-item batches and add unit tests. Any preference on whether helper should always return list-of-list or mirror server response?

anya: Make it list-of-list (explicit is safer for retrievers that expect batch-of-vectors). Document contract in helper docstring and add sampleapp e2e asserting Node & Py normalized outputs match.

kevin: I'll update auth middleware to carry x-rw-idempotency-token across retries and add an integration test that ensures a retried request is deduped on the server side.

morgan: Thanks — once the three PRs land we should update onboarding notes in docs to mention the possible rerank key variance and the helpers' expected shape. That should cut down on new user friction.

infra-bot: DEVEX-2729 updated: assigned to reza (node-batchfix), anya (sdk-mapping), kevin (auth-fix). Please add e2e tests to sampleapp and ping me when PRs reference this ticket.

morgan: will do, thanks everyone. :+1:
